    <h3 class="instructions-heading">General Instructions</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Attempt all questions.</li>
        <li>Write answers clearly and in your own words.</li>
        <li>Marks for each question are indicated alongside it.</li>
        <li>Support your answers with suitable examples wherever required.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3 class="section-heading">Section A: Multiple-Choice Questions</h3>
    <p><strong>Answer all questions. (5 × 1 = 5 Marks)</strong></p>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q1.</strong> Accounting is commonly known as the:
        <br>(a) Language of business
        <br>(b) Language of science
        <br>(c) Language of politics
        <br>(d) Language of law
        <br><span class="marks">[1 Mark]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q2.</strong> Which concept treats the business and its owner as separate entities?
        <br>(a) Going concern concept
        <br>(b) Business entity concept
        <br>(c) Consistency convention
        <br>(d) Money measurement concept
        <br><span class="marks">[1 Mark]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q3.</strong> Which of the following is an external user of accounting information?
        <br>(a) Production manager
        <br>(b) Sales manager
        <br>(c) Bank
        <br>(d) Store supervisor
        <br><span class="marks">[1 Mark]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q4.</strong> The going concern concept assumes that a business:
        <br>(a) Will close immediately
        <br>(b) Will continue its operations for the foreseeable future
        <br>(c) Will never earn a profit
        <br>(d) Will avoid all liabilities
        <br><span class="marks">[1 Mark]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q5.</strong> Which of the following is a main purpose of an accounting information system?
        <br>(a) To collect and process financial data
        <br>(b) To eliminate all business risks
        <br>(c) To guarantee profits
        <br>(d) To replace every management decision
        <br><span class="marks">[1 Mark]</span>
    </div>

    <h3 class="section-heading">Section B: Short-Answer Questions</h3>
    <p><strong>Answer all questions. (3 × 2 = 6 Marks)</strong></p>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q6.</strong> Define financial accounting and state any two objectives.
        <br><span class="marks">[2 Marks]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q7.</strong> What is meant by the consistency convention?
        <br><span class="marks">[2 Marks]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q8.</strong> Identify any two users of accounting information and state their information needs.
        <br><span class="marks">[2 Marks]</span>
    </div>

    <h3 class="section-heading">Section C: Descriptive Questions</h3>
    <p><strong>Answer any two questions. (2 × 3 = 6 Marks)</strong></p>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q9.</strong> Explain accounting as the language of business.
        <br><span class="marks">[3 Marks]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q10.</strong> Explain any three accounting concepts, conventions or postulates with examples.
        <br><span class="marks">[3 Marks]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q11.</strong> Explain the role of accounting in economic development.
        <br><span class="marks">[3 Marks]</span>
    </div>

    <h3 class="section-heading">Section D: Application-Based Question</h3>
    <p><strong>Answer the following question. (1 × 3 = 3 Marks)</strong></p>

    <div class="question">
        <strong>Q12.</strong> A business owner pays personal household expenses
        using business funds and records them as business expenses.

        <br><br>
        (a) Identify the accounting concept involved.
        <br>
        (b) Explain why the personal and business transactions should be separated.
        <br>
        (c) State one benefit of maintaining proper accounting records.

        <br><span class="marks">[3 Marks]</span>
    </div>

